  "sticker": "mushroom",
  "skeleton": "mushroom: root at the stem's foot (in the ground); stem bone with squash (the face is on it: eyes, mouth); cap on top of the stem (tips, bounces, lifts).",
  "sheets": [
    {
      "id": "parts",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a mushroom character. Draw this exact mushroom as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate body parts laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every part at the size it has in image 1.\n\nDraw each part on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no part touching or overlapping another:\n1. the cap: the red cap with its white spots and the cream gills underneath, alone, tilted a little as in image 1.\n2. the stem: the plump cream stem with a completely blank face — no eyes, no mouth — keep the rosy cheeks; its top, normally under the cap, rounded.\n\nEvery part is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another part, and each joint end (where it tucks under the body or the head) is a full, smooth, rounded edge. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the parts beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows. Fully transparent background."
    },
    {
      "id": "face",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "references": [
        "parts"
      ],
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a mushroom character; image 2 shows the same mushroom cut into puppet parts, with a blank face. Draw the mushroom's face pieces as separate stickers on one sheet: the same drawing style, colours and line as in image 1, every piece at the size it has on the mushroom in image 1, so it fits the blank face in image 2.\n\nDraw each piece on its own, spread out in tidy rows with wide empty gaps between them, nothing touching:\n1. the mushroom's left eye (on the right of image 1) as it is in image 1: a small dark round eye with a white sparkle.\n2. the same eye wide open and surprised: bigger and rounder, with its white sparkle.\n3. the same eye gently closed in sleep: a soft downward-curving line with a few lashes.\n4. the same eye closed in a happy smile: an upward-curving arc.\n5. the same eye sad: looking down, its upper lid tilted up towards the middle.\n6. the same eye scrunched shut tight, about to sneeze.\n7. the mouth as it is in image 1: a small shy smile.\n8. the mouth pressed tight with puffed cheeks, holding a sneeze.\n9. the mouth wide open in a big happy laugh, the inside pink.\n10. the mouth open in a small round 'o'.\n11. the mouth in a small sad frown.\n\nNo text, no labels, no numbers, no shadows, no face or head around the pieces. Fully transparent background."
    }
